{"kind":"assert","text":"Addition to 9ecd3efa: the cutover family also admits an ordinary\napplication package. Add it to the head plan as a fourth change.\n\nWhat a read of main fdd1c758 found:\n- Rules 10 refuses a package unless it declares exactly one\n  `device-command@1` capability\n  (device-application-rules.ts:45 to 47,\n  device-application-package.ts:10). Commons Rules 14 reuses those\n  rules (commons-rules.ts:20).\n- The Worker-side admission accepts a package with no capability\n  (applications/admission.ts:34 to 37).\n- An ordinary package installs only in the families of register 12\n  and register 13, and a new plan cannot select them\n  (docs/cli.md:243 to 257).\nSo no room that a current Worker creates installs Counter or\nLending as packed by `dap pack`. docs/run-your-app.md:11 says so.\n\nDecision: the new Rules version of the cutover family accepts an\nordinary version 2 package beside a device-command package. The\nfamily's Directory, Register and Destination pin it. I do not\nreadmit the register 13 family, because it has no archive binding\nand would be a second code line.\n\nIn the head plan, give for this change:\n1. the Rules version, the install proof that it accepts, and the\n   files that change.\n2. the witness: `apps/counter` packed by `dap pack` installs in a\n   room of the new family, takes one act and replays. A\n   device-command package still installs.\n3. what the host needs: an `APPLICATION_CONTENT` bucket and the\n   `APPLICATION_TRUST` rows. dap-demo has a trust list and no\n   bucket today (wrangler.demo.jsonc:20). I make that\n   configuration change with the cutover deployment.\n4. the cost of one more option, as a separate line and not as part\n   of the plan: a trust row that names a publisher key and admits\n   every release that the key signs. Today each release needs its\n   own row and so a new Worker version. State what the option\n   changes in admission.ts and what an operator then trusts. The\n   owner decides it.\n\nThis stays a read-only plan. Its priority does not change: behind\nF, G, H and identifiers head (b).","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}